{title: 042 - Now That the Daylight Fills the Sky}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Worship}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[D]Now that the daylight [G]fills [F#m]the [Bm]sky,
[F#m]We lift [Bm]our [D]hearts [A/E]to God [D]on [Bm]high,
[F#m/C#]That [Bm]He, [G]in [A]all we [G]do or [Em]say,
[A7]Would keep [Bm]us free [G]from harm [D/F#]today;

Verse 2:
[D]Would guard our hearts [Bm]and [G]tongues [F#m]from [Bm]strife;
[F#m]From anger's [D]din [A/E]would shield [D]our [Bm]life;
[F#m/C#]From [Bm]evil [A]sights would [G]turn our [Em]eyes,
[A7]And close [Bm]our ears [G]to vanities;

Verse 3:
[D]So we, when this [G]new day [F#m]is [Bm]gone
[F#m]And night [Bm]in [D]turn [A/E]is drawing [Bm]on,
[F#m/C#]With [Bm]conscience [A]by the [G]world unstained
[A7]Shall praise [Bm]His name [G]for vict'ry [D/F#]gained.

Verse 4:
[D]"All praise to [Bm]You, [G]creator [Bm]Lord!
[F#m]All praise [Bm]to [D]You, [A/E]eternal [Bm]Word!
[F#m/C#]All [Bm]praise [G]to [A]You, O [G]Spirit [Em]wise!"
[A7]We sing [Bm]as daylight [G]fills [D/F#]the skies.
